{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","version":"2.1.0","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"CodeQL","organization":"GitHub","semanticVersion":"2.25.4","notifications":[{"id":"py/baseline/expected-extracted-files","name":"py/baseline/expected-extracted-files","shortDescription":{"text":"Expected extracted files"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Files appearing in the source archive that are expected to be extracted."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true},"properties":{"tags":["expected-extracted-files","telemetry"]}},{"id":"cli/file-coverage-baseline","name":"cli/file-coverage-baseline","shortDescription":{"text":"File coverage baseline telemetry"},"fullDescription":{"text":"File coverage baseline telemetry"},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true}},{"id":"cli/platform","name":"cli/platform","shortDescription":{"text":"Platform"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Platform"},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true}}],"rules":[{"id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/xss-jinja2","name":"githubsecuritylab/audit/xss-jinja2","shortDescription":{"text":"Audit: Cross-site scripting using Flask Jinja2 templates"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Templates are vulnerable to cross-site scripting if they are rendered with untrusted data."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"help":{"text":"# Audit: Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) sink in Flask using Jinja2 templates\n\nThis query detects the use of XSS sinks in Flask using Jinja2 templates. XSS sinks are functions that render user input as HTML and if the input is not properly sanitized, it may allow an attacker to execute arbitrary JavaScript code.\n\n## Disclaimer\n\nCodeQL does not support Jinja2 templates out of the box so it does not follow the the data to the Jinja2 sink. It is not guaranteed to find all XSS sinks in Flask applications.\n","markdown":"# Audit: Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) sink in Flask using Jinja2 templates\n\nThis query detects the use of XSS sinks in Flask using Jinja2 templates. XSS sinks are functions that render user input as HTML and if the input is not properly sanitized, it may allow an attacker to execute arbitrary JavaScript code.\n\n## Disclaimer\n\nCodeQL does not support Jinja2 templates out of the box so it does not follow the the data to the Jinja2 sink. It is not guaranteed to find all XSS sinks in Flask applications.\n"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-079","audit"],"description":"Templates are vulnerable to cross-site scripting if they are\n              rendered with untrusted data.","id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/xss-jinja2","kind":"path-problem","name":"Audit: Cross-site scripting using Flask Jinja2 templates","precision":"very-low","problem.severity":"warning","security-severity":"2.5","sub-severity":"low"}},{"id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/unsafe-deserialization","name":"githubsecuritylab/audit/unsafe-deserialization","shortDescription":{"text":"Audit: Usage of Deserializing function"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Deserializing user-controlled data may allow attackers to execute arbitrary code."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"help":{"text":"# Audit: Usage of Deserializing function\n\nThis query detects the use of deserializing functions. Deserializing functions are functions that deserialize data and if the data is constructed using user input, it may allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code.\n","markdown":"# Audit: Usage of Deserializing function\n\nThis query detects the use of deserializing functions. Deserializing functions are functions that deserialize data and if the data is constructed using user input, it may allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code.\n"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-502","audit"],"description":"Deserializing user-controlled data may allow attackers to execute arbitrary code.","id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/unsafe-deserialization","kind":"problem","name":"Audit: Usage of Deserializing function","precision":"very-low","problem.severity":"warning","security-severity":"2.5","sub-severity":"low"}},{"id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/xxe-local-file","name":"githubsecuritylab/audit/xxe-local-file","shortDescription":{"text":"Audit: Usage of Insecure XML Parser"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Parsing XML using an insecure parser can lead to security issues."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"error"},"help":{"text":"# Audit: Usage of Insecure XML Parser\n\nThis query detects the use of insecure XML parsers. Insecure XML parsers are parsers that do not prevent XML External Entity (XXE) attacks. If an XML parser is used to parse untrusted user input, it may allow an attacker to perform XXE attacks.\n","markdown":"# Audit: Usage of Insecure XML Parser\n\nThis query detects the use of insecure XML parsers. Insecure XML parsers are parsers that do not prevent XML External Entity (XXE) attacks. If an XML parser is used to parse untrusted user input, it may allow an attacker to perform XXE attacks.\n"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-611","external/cwe/cwe-776","external/cwe/cwe-827","external/cwe/cwe-502","audit"],"description":"Parsing XML using an insecure parser can lead to security issues.","id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/xxe-local-file","kind":"problem","name":"Audit: Usage of Insecure XML Parser","precision":"high","problem.severity":"error","security-severity":"6.0"}},{"id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/code-injection","name":"githubsecuritylab/audit/code-injection","shortDescription":{"text":"Audit: Usage of Code Injection sink"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Interpreting unsanitized user input as code allows a malicious user to perform arbitrary code execution."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"help":{"text":"# Audit: Usage of Code Injection sink\n\nThis query detects the use of code injection sinks. Code injection sinks are functions that execute code and if the code is constructed using user input, it may allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code.\n","markdown":"# Audit: Usage of Code Injection sink\n\nThis query detects the use of code injection sinks. Code injection sinks are functions that execute code and if the code is constructed using user input, it may allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code.\n"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-094","external/cwe/cwe-095","external/cwe/cwe-116","audit"],"description":"Interpreting unsanitized user input as code allows a malicious user to perform arbitrary\n              code execution.","id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/code-injection","kind":"problem","name":"Audit: Usage of Code Injection sink","precision":"very-low","problem.severity":"warning","security-severity":"2.5","sub-severity":"low"}},{"id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/command-line-injection","name":"githubsecuritylab/audit/command-line-injection","shortDescription":{"text":"Audit: Usage of Command Injection sink"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Using externally controlled strings in a command line may allow a malicious user to change the meaning of the command."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"help":{"text":"# Audit: Usage of Command Injection sink\n\nThis query detects the use of command injection sinks. Command injection sinks are functions that execute a command in a shell and if the command is constructed using user input, it may allow an attacker to execute arbitrary commands.\n","markdown":"# Audit: Usage of Command Injection sink\n\nThis query detects the use of command injection sinks. Command injection sinks are functions that execute a command in a shell and if the command is constructed using user input, it may allow an attacker to execute arbitrary commands.\n"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-078","external/cwe/cwe-088","audit"],"description":"Using externally controlled strings in a command line may allow a malicious\n              user to change the meaning of the command.","id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/command-line-injection","kind":"problem","name":"Audit: Usage of Command Injection sink","precision":"very-low","problem.severity":"warning","security-severity":"2.5","sub-severity":"low"}},{"id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/sql-injection","name":"githubsecuritylab/audit/sql-injection","shortDescription":{"text":"SQL query built from user-controlled sources"},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"help":{"text":"# Audit - SQL Injection using format strings\n\nDynamically generated SQL queries using format strings can cause SQL injection attacks. The following example shows how to use the `sql` package to execute a query with a format string:\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Format string\nquery = f\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '{username}'\"\ncursor.execute(query)\n\n# str.format()\nquery = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '{}'\".format(username)\ncursor.execute(query)\n\n# \"%s\" % string\nquery = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = %s\" % username\ncursor.execute(query)\n```\n","markdown":"# Audit - SQL Injection using format strings\n\nDynamically generated SQL queries using format strings can cause SQL injection attacks. The following example shows how to use the `sql` package to execute a query with a format string:\n\n## Example\n\n```python\n# Format string\nquery = f\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '{username}'\"\ncursor.execute(query)\n\n# str.format()\nquery = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '{}'\".format(username)\ncursor.execute(query)\n\n# \"%s\" % string\nquery = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = %s\" % username\ncursor.execute(query)\n```\n"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-089","audit"],"id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/sql-injection","kind":"path-problem","name":"SQL query built from user-controlled sources","precision":"very-low","problem.severity":"warning","security-severity":"2.5","sub-severity":"low"}},{"id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/sql-injection","name":"githubsecuritylab/audit/sql-injection","shortDescription":{"text":"SQL query built from user-controlled sources"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Building a SQL query from user-controlled sources is vulnerable to insertion of malicious SQL code by the user."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"error"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-089","heuristic","audit"],"description":"Building a SQL query from user-controlled sources is vulnerable to insertion of\n              malicious SQL code by the user.","id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/sql-injection","kind":"path-problem","name":"SQL query built from user-controlled sources","precision":"high","problem.severity":"error","security-severity":"8.8"}},{"id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/dangerous-functions","name":"githubsecuritylab/audit/dangerous-functions","shortDescription":{"text":"Audit: Usage of Dangerous Functions"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Dangerous Functions"},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"warning"},"help":{"text":"# Audit: Usage of Dangerous Functions\n\nThis query detects the use of dangerous functions. Dangerous functions are functions that are known to be dangerous if used in applications.\n","markdown":"# Audit: Usage of Dangerous Functions\n\nThis query detects the use of dangerous functions. Dangerous functions are functions that are known to be dangerous if used in applications.\n"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-676","audit"],"description":"Dangerous Functions","id":"githubsecuritylab/audit/dangerous-functions","kind":"problem","name":"Audit: Usage of Dangerous Functions","precision":"low","problem.severity":"warning","security-severity":"2.5","sub-severity":"low"}},{"id":"py/untrusted-data-to-external-api","name":"py/untrusted-data-to-external-api","shortDescription":{"text":"Untrusted data passed to external API"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Data provided remotely is used in this external API without sanitization, which could be a security risk."},"defaultConfiguration":{"enabled":true,"level":"error"},"properties":{"tags":["security","external/cwe/cwe-020"],"description":"Data provided remotely is used in this external API without sanitization, which could be a security risk.","id":"py/untrusted-data-to-external-api","kind":"path-problem","name":"Untrusted data passed to external API","precision":"low","problem.severity":"error","security-severity":"7.8"}}]},"extensions":[{"name":"githubsecuritylab/codeql-python-queries","semanticVersion":"0.6.0+38d1f1a395b1768d99fec9468c44b6971a373ed8","locations":[{"uri":"file:///home/ubuntu/.codeql/packages/githubsecuritylab/codeql-python-queries/0.6.0/","description":{"text":"The QL pack root directory."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackRoot"]}},{"uri":"file:///home/ubuntu/.codeql/packages/githubsecuritylab/codeql-python-queries/0.6.0/qlpack.yml","description":{"text":"The QL pack definition file."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackDefinitionFile"]}}]},{"name":"codeql/python-all","semanticVersion":"7.1.2+1a82a682e9750929a11872d8456ff91e90fc6352","locations":[{"uri":"file:///home/ubuntu/.codeql/packages/githubsecuritylab/codeql-python-queries/0.6.0/.codeql/libraries/codeql/python-all/7.1.2/","description":{"text":"The QL pack root directory."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackRoot"]}},{"uri":"file:///home/ubuntu/.codeql/packages/githubsecuritylab/codeql-python-queries/0.6.0/.codeql/libraries/codeql/python-all/7.1.2/qlpack.yml","description":{"text":"The QL pack definition file."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackDefinitionFile"]}}]},{"name":"codeql/threat-models","semanticVersion":"1.0.51+1a82a682e9750929a11872d8456ff91e90fc6352","locations":[{"uri":"file:///home/ubuntu/.codeql/packages/githubsecuritylab/codeql-python-queries/0.6.0/.codeql/libraries/codeql/threat-models/1.0.51/","description":{"text":"The QL pack root directory."},"properties":{"tags":["CodeQL/LocalPackRoot"]}},{"uri":"file:///home/ubuntu/.codeql/packages/githubsecuritylab/codeql-python-queries/0.6.0/.codeql/libraries/codeql/threat-models/1.0.51/